[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Every project starts clean in your head and then reality hits. The brief is in one document. The feedback is in a spreadsheet. The meeting notes are messy. The competitor research is scattered across tabs and somehow you'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'still need to turn all of that into a strategy presentation, summary, tracker, and plan your team can use. Now, this is where AutoMind AI becomes really useful.'

[00:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Instead of asking a chatbot for one answer and doing the rest yourself, you can give AutoMind AI the whole problem, the files, the contact, the goal, and the deliverables. But, before I start'

[00:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the workflow, I wanted to show you guys the model selector. The platform includes AutoMind Light, AutoMind Pro, Gemini 5.6, Soul, Gemini 5.6 Pro, Gemini 5.6 Luna, Claude Fable 5, Claude Sonnet'

[00:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '5, and GLM 5.2. Plenty of models to choose from. But, for this workflow, I would choose Claude Sonnet 5 because'

[01:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'this job needs reasoning, writing, planning, and file understanding. Now, here\'s the case study. Imagine I am preparing a launch strategy for a meal planning app for busy professionals,'

[01:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'right? Now, the team sent a rough product brief, an early feedback spreadsheet, as well competitor links, and messy planning notes, right? My goal is not just to ask, "What should we do?"'

[01:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'My goal is to create a complete launch package. So, here\'s the prompt I would use. I\'m launching a meal planning application for busy professionals. Use the uploaded brief, feedback'

[01:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'spreadsheet, planning notes, and competitor research links. Create a launch with positioning, audience segments, key messages, channel plan, timeline, risks, and next steps, right?'

[01:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And then turn the result into an editable presentation and a one-page executive summary. Now, that prompt works because it gives AutoMind AI three things: a task, context, and output. It'

[02:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'is not a random question, it is real work. And this is the main difference. AutoMind AI is not only a general AI assistant, it combines AI chat file'

[02:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'workspace, web research, document creation, spreadsheet analysis, presentation generation, visual creation, file management, integrations, and scheduled automation. Now, the first'

[02:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'step is file understanding, right? So, I\'m going to upload the brief, the spreadsheet, and the notes I have. Instead of reading everything manually, I ask AutoMind AI to summarize what matters. Now, from the brief, I want the'

[02:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'product promise, the target user, the pricing idea, and launch constraints, right? And spreadsheet, I want feedback patterns, complaints, maybe the benefits as well, the red flags. And from the'

[03:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'notes, I want decisions, open questions, and action items. Now, this is where the workspace matters. The files are not just attachments in a temporary chat. AutoMind AI can browse saved files,'

[03:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'search files by name, type, date, size, or folders. It can open files for analysis, attach existing files into a conversation, and help replace a saved'

[03:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'file with an edited version. So, next week, I don\'t have to rebuild the context from zero. The second step is research. I ask AutoMind AI to search the web and compare similar meal'

[03:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'planning, fitness, and productivity apps. I want to know what competitor promise, what audiences they target, what features they highlight, and where the gaps are. Automone AI can search the'

[03:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'public web, read web pages, and use current information when needed. So, this strategy is not based only on old notes. Next, I\'ll ask it to create a launch'

[04:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'strategy. I want it structured like a real business document, right? I want overview, target audience, positioning, and key messages, launch channels as well, timeline, risks, and'

[04:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'recommendations. Now, this turns messy inputs into a clear plan. I like it. Then, I continue the workflow by saying, "Turn the strategy into a six-slide editable deck, right?" The slides should'

[04:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'include a title slide, market insight, target audience, launch message, channel, timeline, and next steps. Automone AI can create editable slide decks, generate presentation content and'

[04:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'structure, support editing inside the Automone editor, and export when requested. Now, that means the output becomes something I can present. And if I want the deck to look more visual, I'

[04:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'can create a hero asset. Automone AI can generate images from text prompt, edit or restart uploaded images, create posters, covers, icons, product visuals, and help decide whether an image should'

[05:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'be generated, searched publicly, or drawn as an editable graphic. After the deck, I ask for a one-page executive summary. Now, this is useful because not everyone wants to open the whole'

[05:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'presentation. Automone AI can create Word documents, summarize docx files, rewrite and reformat documents, and generate reports, proposals, meeting notes, contracts, and drafts. So, I can reuse the same context for a leadership'

[05:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'summary, client memo, or internal handoff. Now, I move to the spreadsheet side, right? So, I ask OtterMind to create a launch budget and KPI tracker with columns for channel owner budget,'

[05:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'target audience, expected reach, conversation goal, launch date, status, and even notes, right? So, it can read and analyze Excel, CSV, TSV, and spreadsheet files. As well, it can'

[06:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'create XLSX files, edit spreadsheet structure and data, validate formulas, and repair broken formulas. That helps with budgets, forecasts, audits, payroll, reports, and financial models.'

[06:17] [scene:talk]
